{"id":"lock","name":"Lock","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:lock"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Lock","text":"The Hebrews usually secured their doors by bars of wood or iron (Isa. 45:2; 1 Kings 4:3). These were the locks originally used, and were opened and shut by large keys applied through an opening in the outside (Judg. 3:24). (See KEY.) Lock of hair (Judg. 16:13, 19; Ezek. 8:3; Num. 6:5, etc.)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1817","lemma":"דֶּלֶת","xlit":"deleth","gloss":"something swinging","kjv":"door, gate, leaf, lid","count":5,"share":0.83},{"strong":"H4514","lemma":"מַנְעוּל","xlit":"manʻûwl","gloss":"a bolt","kjv":"lock","count":3,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H5944","lemma":"עֲלִיָּה","xlit":"ʻălîyâh","gloss":"something lofty","kjv":"ascent, chamber, going up, loft","count":3,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H5274","lemma":"נָעַל","xlit":"nâʻal","gloss":"to fasten up","kjv":"bolt, inclose, lock, shoe","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H830","lemma":"אַשְׁפֹּת","xlit":"ʼashpôth","gloss":"a heap of rubbish or filth","kjv":"dung","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H1280","lemma":"בְּרִיחַ","xlit":"bᵉrîyach","gloss":"a bolt","kjv":"bar, fugitive","count":2,"share":0.33}],"verses":["Judg.3.23","Judg.3.24","Judg.3.25","Neh.3.13","Neh.3.14","Song.5.5"],"related":[{"id":"eglon","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.12,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"gilgal","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.035,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"deception","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.022,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"door","type":"lexical","strong":"H1817","why":"both lead with דֶּלֶת (H1817)"},{"id":"gates","type":"lexical","strong":"H1817","why":"both lead with דֶּלֶת (H1817)"}],"works":[{"work":"callaway","title":"The Religious System of the Amazulu","count":5,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Amazulu.4","count":4,"book":"Callaway","title":"Amatongo; or, Ancestor Worship"},{"chapter":"Amazulu.1